  "summary": "A fairly common summer resident. A large cuckoo with a crested grey head, white-spotted black upper parts and creamy-white underparts. The immature has a black cap, a shorter crest and chestnut-brown primaries. The common call is a rasping keeow, repeated in phrases of about eight. It parasitises crows and starlings. Months were left unset. The Kemp code VB was left unchanged.",
